DTSTAMP:20270508T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270508
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270509
SUMMARY:First Aid\, Adult CPR\, and AED
DESCRIPTION:First Aid\, Adult CPR\, and AED\nSave the Date\nTopics include
 :\nAdult CPR and The Emergency Action Steps\nAutomated External Defibrill
 ator (AED) and Prioritizing Care\nUse of Barrier devices… Bleeding Cont
 rol…Tourniquets\nConscious and Unconscious Choking\, Burns and Shock\nH
 eat and Cold related emergencies and Sudden Illness\nInjuries to muscles\
 , bones and joints\nParticipants should:\nbe at least 15 years of age (ex
 ceptions can be made by training coordinator)\nbe able to complete strenu
 ous activities (such as bending\, lifting\, kneeling\, etc)\nAs a result 
 of the course\, participants will complete:\nFirst Aid and receive a 2-ye
 ar card.\nCPR and receive a 2-year card.\nThis course DOES NOT provide:\n
 First aid merit badge - Infant CPR training\nNOTE: CPR or First Aid may b
 e taken separately but the cost is the same for all or part of a class. T
 he exact start time of First Aid varies. CPR typically lasts 3 hours.\n\n
 https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-may-2027
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-may-20
 27
